# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
#
# CRDroid Android 16 (raphael / SM8150) fragment.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This fragment is now intentionally EMPTY of options, and that is the point.
#
# Earlier revisions of this file added a set of "parity with the ROM's 4.14
# kernel" options (CRYPTO_GCM, TMPFS_POSIX_ACL, PSTORE_*, BLK_WBT) plus a block
# of display options (DRM_MSM, FB, DSI PHYs). Every one of those was a wrong
# inference, and the display block was actively destructive:
#
#   * raphael's panel driver is NOT drivers/gpu/drm/msm. It lives in
#     techpack/display/msm/ and is pulled in by CONFIG_MSM_EXT_DISPLAY, which
#     the base defconfig already sets. The dsi_gen stack under
#     drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/ is a different, unused generation.
#   * Setting CONFIG_DRM_MSM=y builds drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c alongside
#     techpack/display/msm/msm_drv.c -- two drivers claiming the same name.
#   * The author's own released kernel, which boots, has
#     "# CONFIG_DRM_MSM is not set" and "# CONFIG_FB is not set".
#
# The authoritative reference is now the config the maintainer shipped, extracted
# from the released Image.gz via its embedded IKCFG payload. The build seeds from
# that file directly; see build/build-kernel.sh. Nothing here needs overriding.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The ONE override that matters on CRDroid A16: drop ramoops_memreserve from
# the built-in cmdline. The author.config seed carries
#   CONFIG_CMDLINE="cgroup_disable=pressure ramoops_memreserve=4M"
# and the 5.4 DTB *also* has a ramoops reserved-memory node at 0xB0000000, so
# both mechanisms register a pstore console on the same window ("OF: reserved
# mem: OVERLAP DETECTED! ramoops@B0000000 overlaps with ramoops@B0000000").
# Removing the cmdline parameter leaves exactly one pstore instance -- the DTB
# node.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_CMDLINE="cgroup_disable=pressure"
CONFIG_CMDLINE_EXTEND=y

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROM parity, userspace-critical.  The 4.14 kernel that actually boots this
# ROM (verified: boot_completed=1) has all three of these =y; the author's
# seed config has them =n, and with that setting the boot dies like this:
#
#   * this tree has no devtmpfs (CONFIG_DEVTMPFS=n in both configs), so the
#     userspace's /dev is a tmpfs that ueventd populates with mknod/symlink;
#   * without tmpfs xattr support SELinux cannot attach the security.selinux
#     label to a file created there and the creation fails with EOPNOTSUPP;
#   * /dev/block/by-name/* therefore never appears, init's
#       "reboot-bootloader: ... failed to stat /dev/block/bootdevice/by-name/misc"
#     is the visible symptom, and apexd cannot open the loop/dm devices its
#     bootstrap needs;
#   * the failed "apexd-bootstrap" oneshot trips apexd.rc's
#       reboot_on_failure reboot,bootloader,bootstrap-apexd-failed
#     and the phone reboots to fastboot ~12.5 s into the boot.
#
# CONFIG_SYSFS_SYSCALL is the deprecated sysfs(2) call; bionic's fstab and
# mount helpers fall back to it, and the ROM's kernel enables it.
CONFIG_TMPFS_XATTR=y
CONFIG_TMPFS_POSIX_ACL=y
CONFIG_SYSFS_SYSCALL=y
# /data is f2fs with file-based encryption and has to keep working.  This
# tree integrates f2fs FBE through the generic fscrypt framework: fs/f2fs/
# Kconfig selects F2FS_FS_XATTR/FS_ENCRYPTION_ALGS "if FS_ENCRYPTION" and the
# f2fs sources test CONFIG_FS_ENCRYPTION -- there is no f2fs-private
# encryption symbol in this tree.  (An earlier revision of this fragment set
# CONFIG_F2FS_FS_ENCRYPTION, which does not exist here and was silently
# dropped by olddefconfig.)  The author's seed already carries
# CONFIG_FS_ENCRYPTION=y and CONFIG_FS_ENCRYPTION_INLINE_CRYPT=y, and the
# result is verified on the device: ro.crypto.state=encrypted /
# ro.crypto.type=file with /data mounting normally.

# The "schedtune" cgroup v1 controller, required by the ROM's userspace:
# init.rc creates /dev/stune/* and libprocessgroup's SetupCgroups aborts the
# whole boot when the controller cannot be mounted (every service start then
# fails in createProcessGroup and init reboots as "bootstrap-apexd-failed"
# ~10 s in).  The 4.14 stock kernel has CONFIG_SCHED_TUNE=y; the RaphGhost
# 5.4 tree does not carry the driver, so kernel/sched/tune.c ports the
# control interface (attributes only, no scheduler hooks).  Implemented in
# this tree; see the comment there.
CONFIG_SCHED_TUNE=y
